# Target C-II — uniform support-six `H5` exclusion by projection potentials

**Date:** 2026-09-18  
**Status:** proved candidate awaiting independent audit; theorem-state authority unchanged  
**Scope:** the six noncollapsed uniform support-six reciprocal `H5` sign/order orbits  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_support6_h5_uniform_projection_potential_2026_09_18.py`

This note eliminates the six uniform `H5` metric cases left by the exact
support-six sign/order reduction. It does not address the ten simple-wall cases,
the collapsed support-six branch, or higher-codimension strata beyond the already
promoted double-wall exclusion.

The dependency chain is

```text
uniform H5 finite reduction
  -> six exact sign/chirotope representatives
  -> all generic projection orders of each uniform order type
  -> no acyclic signed projection constraint graph
  -> contradiction with full signed unit-force equilibrium
  -> uniform H5 eliminated; ten simple-wall H5 cases remain.
```

## The projection-potential lemma

Let `E` be the present reciprocal edges, let `s_ij` be their nonzero reciprocal
signs, and put

\[
 e_{ij}=\frac{y_i-y_j}{|y_i-y_j|},\qquad
 F_i=\sum_{j:ij\in E}s_{ij}e_{ij}.
\]

The six physical pentagon closures give `F_i=0` for every non-ground reciprocal
vertex. Endpoint cancellation then gives the ground equation as well. For any
scalar vertex potential `a` and any vector `u`, therefore,

\[
 0=\sum_i a_i\,u\!\cdot F_i
  =\sum_{ij\in E}s_{ij}(a_i-a_j)
    \frac{u\!\cdot(y_i-y_j)}{|y_i-y_j|}.
\tag{1}
\]

Fix a generic `u` and write `x_i=u\cdot y_i`. Direct every present edge so that
the desired inequality is

\[
 a_i>a_j\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
 s_{ij}(x_i-x_j)>0.
\tag{2}
\]

If this directed graph is acyclic, choose `a` strictly increasing along its
edges. Every summand in (1) is then strictly positive, a contradiction. Thus a
necessary condition for a metric reciprocal equilibrium is:

\[
\boxed{\text{for every generic projection order, the signed constraint graph
must contain a directed cycle.}}
\tag{3}
\]

This is a purely finite consequence of the full equilibrium equations. It uses
no trace approximation or numerical optimization.

## Exact finite check

The coordinate certificate in the companion verifier is a useful sanity check:
each stored integer realization has exactly the target 35 triple signs and has
40 generic projection sectors, with no acyclic signed constraint graph. The
coordinate-free certificate is stronger and is the authoritative finite check.

It adjoins a formal point `U` at infinity and enumerates all `7!` possible
projection orders. For each order it assigns
`chi(U,i,j)=sign(x_j-x_i)` and checks every rank-three
Grassmann--Pluecker axiom on the eight-element extension. Every realizable
generic projection order passes these tests, so this is an overapproximation of
all metric projection orders. None of the valid extensions has an acyclic signed
constraint graph. This avoids any dependence on one sampled coordinate
realization or on an unproved realizability claim for the finite enumeration.

The verifier reports:

\[
\boxed{6\text{ uniform orbits},\quad
\text{rank-three infinity extensions }(140,140,146,152,152,156),
\quad 0\text{ acyclic orders}.}
\]

Consequently every uniform H5 metric realization would violate (1), so the six
uniform cases are excluded.

## Scope and remaining task

The result is a proof-only candidate, not a canonical theorem-state promotion.
The next finite task is the ten simple-wall `H5` orbits. Their nonuniform
chirotopes require a separate treatment of projection orders with the wall
degeneracy and cannot be silently covered by this uniform certificate. The
collapsed all-equal support-six local family also remains live; its certified
local realization prevents an exclusion based only on the already imposed local
pentagon conditions.

If the ten wall cases and collapsed branch are both removed, the support-six
endpoint is excluded and the one-anchor coefficient can be propagated from
`n_1/6` to `n_1/7` through the existing FREE inequalities. This note alone does
not justify that propagation.

**Disposition:** proved candidate awaiting independent audit; uniform H5 branch
closed within the stated full-equilibrium hypotheses; C-II remains open.
